Plain-language summary
- You may use, copy, modify, and distribute DarijaCode (the “Project”) for any purpose, including commercial use.
- You must keep this license and give visible credit to the original project.
- You must not present a copy or fork as the official DarijaCode project. Community forks must identify themselves as a community fork and use a community name (see §4).
- If the Maintainer is inactive for 6 months, the community is explicitly permitted to continue the Project as a clearly labeled community fork.
- The Project is provided “as is” with no warranty.

Full terms

1. Definitions
1.1 “Project” means the source code, documentation, and files contained in this repository.
1.2 “You” means any person or organization using, copying, modifying, or distributing the Project.
1.3 “Derivative Tool” means software that works alongside the Project (editor, plugin, docs site, linter, package tool, etc.) but is not a redistribution of the Project itself.
1.4 “Maintainer” means the project owner (krnl0xsns1nk) or anyone the Maintainer designates in writing.
1.5 “Community Fork” means a redistribution of the Project that continues development independently while complying with Section 5.

2. Grant of rights
2.1 Subject to these terms, You are granted a worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive license to:
  a) use, reproduce, modify, and distribute the Project in source or binary form; and
  b) create and distribute Derivative Tools under any license You choose.

3. Attribution and redistribution requirements
3.1 Any copy or substantial portion of the Project that You distribute (modified or not) must:
  a) include an unmodified copy of this license file; and
  b) include a visible credit naming the original author (“krnl0xsns1nk”) and a link to the original repository.
3.2 If You distribute a modified version, You must clearly state that the Project was modified.
3.3 If You distribute compiled or binary forms (including for commercial sale), You must either:
  a) include the complete corresponding source code for that exact release, or
  b) include a prominent, permanent link to a freely accessible copy of the exact source (for example, a repository URL and commit/tag),
  and in all cases include this license file.

4. No misrepresentation; naming
4.1 You must not claim authorship of the original Project or present a copy, fork, or modified version as the official DarijaCode project.
4.2 Community forks and redistributions MAY NOT use the exact name “DarijaCode” by itself as their project name or brand. They must choose an identifying name and clearly label themselves as a community fork. Acceptable examples:
  - “MyLang — a community fork of DarijaCode”
  - “Community of DarijaCode — maintained by [group/person]”
4.3 Derivative Tools (editors, plugins, docs sites) may reference DarijaCode and say they are “for DarijaCode” but must not claim they are the original compiler or official project.

5. Community stewardship (inactivity)
5.1 The Maintainer is “active” if they have at least one commit in the canonical repository within the previous six (6) months.
5.2 If the Maintainer is inactive by that measure, the community is explicitly permitted, without further permission, to fork and continue development and releases, provided the community fork:
  a) clearly identifies itself as community-maintained (e.g., “Community of DarijaCode”); and
  b) complies with Sections 3 and 4 (attribution and no misrepresentation).
5.3 This clause does not transfer copyright or ownership; it is a standing permission to avoid blocking continued maintenance.

6. Termination
6.1 Your rights under this license terminate automatically if You materially breach Section 4 and fail to cure the breach within thirty (30) days after written notice.
6.2 Termination does not affect rights previously granted to third parties who received the Project lawfully from You.

7. Disclaimer of warranty and limitation of liability
7.1 The Project is provided “as is,” without warranty of any kind. To the fullest extent allowed by law, the Maintainer and contributors are not liable for any damages arising from use of the Project.

8. Trademarks and other rights
8.1 This license does not grant any trademark rights. Use of the name “DarijaCode” as a trademark or service mark requires separate permission from the Maintainer.
8.2 If You require legal certainty (for commercial or enterprise use), consult a lawyer.

